course: dictionary
lesson: 14906
title: Words that come back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Recurrent describes something that keeps coming back. Its root is «recur», which means to happen again. Look for clues like again, every week, or over and over. «Sam has a recurrent dream about a dark cave.» The dream comes back many times, so recurrent means happening again and again.
explain: Recurrent is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as dream, problem, or headache. «The team had a recurrent problem: the van broke down every week.» Every week is the clue. The problem keeps coming back, so it is recurrent.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «coming back again and again» in place of recurrent. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: «Recurrent» means happening again and again, many times.
fact: «Recurrent headaches» are headaches that keep coming back.
fact: A «recurrent theme» is an idea that appears again and again in a story.
fact: In maths, the usual word for a decimal that repeats forever is «recurring», as in 1 ÷ 3 = 0.333…; «recurrent» carries the same idea of coming back.
fact: Look for clue words such as again, every week, or over and over.
exercise: «Sam has a recurrent nightmare about the dark cave.» What does recurrent mean? | Hidden under the bed | Very frightening, and it happened only once | *Happening again and again | Happy and bright
exercise: «The team had a recurrent problem: the van broke down every week.» What does the word every week suggest? | *The problem keeps coming back | The problem is new and rare | The team won every game | The van is brand new
exercise: Mia writes 1 ÷ 3 = 0.333… Which word is the usual name for a decimal that repeats forever? | Rare | *Recurring | Perfect | Hidden
test: «Her recurrent cough made Mum take her to the doctor.» Which word means the same as recurrent? | Silent | Sleepy | Brand new | *Repeated
test: Jayden says recurrent means rare. What is the best answer? | Right, it means very rare | *Wrong, it means happening again and again, many times | Right, it means happening once | Wrong, it means very loud
exam: «The recurrent noise from the pipes kept waking the baby every night.» What does recurrent mean in this sentence? | Quiet and gentle | Cold and wet | *Happening again and again | Loud and sudden, and it happened only once
